# =============================================================================
# Grant the LSIO `abc` user (uid 911) passwordless sudo.
#
# Why this exists
# ---------------
# The github-actions runner service drops to the unprivileged `abc` user
# (see root/etc/s6-overlay/s6-rc.d/svc-gh-runner/run -- it execs the listener
# under `s6-setuidgid abc`). All job steps therefore run as `abc`, NOT root.
#
# That mirrors the GitHub-hosted ubuntu-latest convention, where the runner
# user is `runner` (non-root) and has unrestricted NOPASSWD sudo via
# /etc/sudoers.d/runner. A huge swath of the GHA ecosystem -- official
# actions, third-party actions, and ad-hoc `run:` blocks alike -- assumes
# `sudo apt-get install ...` Just Works. Without this drop-in, every such
# workflow fails with `sudo: command not found` (exit 127) or
# `abc is not in the sudoers file` (exit 1).
#
# Threat model
# ------------
# This is a *self-hosted* runner image; the operator has already chosen to
# execute arbitrary GHA workloads inside it. Granting `abc` NOPASSWD sudo
# does not meaningfully expand the trust boundary -- a malicious workflow
# step can already exfiltrate any in-container secret, persist files, and
# initiate outbound network calls. The container boundary (and any
# orchestrator-level network/volume policy) is the real enforcement point.
# This is the same posture GitHub themselves use on their hosted fleet.
#
# File-mode requirement
# ---------------------
# sudoers.d files MUST be mode 0440 (owned root:root) or sudo refuses to
# parse them with "/etc/sudoers.d/X is mode 0644, should be 0440". The
# Dockerfile chmods this file to 0440 explicitly after the COPY because
# Docker's COPY preserves the host file mode, which on macOS / non-root
# tooling is typically 0644.
# =============================================================================
abc ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
